{# Empty state for a route whose content is x-show-gated.

   Six routes rendered literally blank with no data -- /app/budget/,
   /app/calendar/, /app/payees/, /app/scheduled/, /app/rules/ and the
   reports -- because their root section is hidden until there is something
   to show, and nothing was rendered in its place. A new user's first sight
   of the budget screen was an empty page with no explanation and no way
   forward.

   Usage -- import the macro, then call it with:
     when    an Alpine expression; the state shows while it is true
     title   one short line
     body    one or two sentences saying what to do next
     cta     optional button label
     action  optional Alpine expression run on click

   Nunjucks comments do not nest, so this block deliberately contains no
   template syntax: a sample with its own comment marker closes THIS
   comment early and the remainder is parsed as markup ("unexpected end of
   comment", which points at the calling page rather than at this file).

   `cta` and `action` are optional -- some routes have nothing useful to
   offer beyond an explanation, and a button that goes nowhere is worse
   than no button. #}

{% macro emptyState(when, title, body, cta, action) %}
<div class="empty-state" x-show="{{ when }}" x-cloak>
  <p class="empty-state__title">{{ title }}</p>
  <p class="empty-state__body">{{ body }}</p>
  {% if cta %}
  <div class="empty-state__actions">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" @click="{{ action }}">{{ cta }}</button>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
